structure corpus: comments, continuation, indented lines, ground and globals
* A star comment line.
; A line that starts with a semicolon is a comment too.
.preprocess replaceground true ; gnd and ground become node 0

Vsupply in gnd 5 ; the supply, with an end-of-line comment
R1 in mid[0] 1k
    an indented line, which Xyce reads as a comment
R2 mid[0] 0
* a comment between a line and the + line that continues it

+ 2k
Rbus $Gbus GROUND 10k
Rtap $gbus mid[0]
  an indented line between a line and its + line does not break the join
+ 4.7k ;a comment needs no blank before it
.global vdd
Vdd vdd 0 3.3
Rdd vdd 0 1meg
	a tab-indented line is a comment as well
.END ; the end of the netlist

